From 67f6d69a623d0688b040f0fba23276b13fc8ae06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:07:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 105/119] fix: SVOGI - the sun goes in at stock units and the
 exposure comes out at the boundary

The shadow filler that did not follow the aperture. Two faults, one subsystem.

The first is an S2 regression that exists with the exposure out of the picture
entirely: the sun colour SVOGI injects is GetSunColor(), and S2 made that
radiometric by moving the 1/PI into the BRDF. 11.90 engine units then go into a
codec whose ceiling is a hard 4.0 (CommonSVO.cfi EncodeHDR packs a shared
exponent into an 8-bit alpha), so every injected texel clipped AND hue-shifted
toward the sun's own chromaticity. 4.0 is not an arbitrary number: CE sized it
against its own photometric sun of 3.788. Both injection sites - the RSM sun
constant in the renderer and the DLF_SUN entry in the 3DEngine's TI light list -
divide the sun back by PI on the scene-referred path, and only the sun; point
lights never carried the divide on either path.

The second is the exposure. The SVO is a cache, and the aperture spans five
decades: no 8-bit shared exponent carries that on top of the scene's own range,
and applying the exposure at injection would put the sun under the codec's 0.25
floor outdoors and sixteen times over its ceiling indoors. So the whole voxel
machine - pools, ceiling, pow(L, 1/booster), the [0,8] trace clamps, DiffuseBias,
every amplifier - keeps seeing exactly the numbers it was tuned against, and the
pre-exposure is applied where GI meets shading instead: ApplyGI() modes 1 and 2
(mode 0 excluded, its texture is an occlusion factor, not a radiance), and the
SVO atmosphere in the fog pass, which is the second output and would otherwise
have become the new exposure-invariant filler. In mode 1 the multiply lands
before the specular ratio so numerator and denominator stay in the same units.

e_svoTI_SSDepthTrace is held at 0 on this path - it is the one place SVOGI reads
an already-exposed buffer back into unexposed voxel maths - and r_HDRDebug 1's
coverage table now reports SVOGI as reached.

research/s8-svogi-units.md, decisions/s8-svogi-fog-clouds.md item 1 approach A.
Off the switch every multiply is an exact 1.0 and both divides are not compiled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A72MFkdSczncE7au9UVnmu
